From: TB371FC Linux port maintainers <tb371fc-desktop@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: qcom: add TB371FC display compatibles

The Lenovo TB371FC uses SM8250 with a board-specific DSI PHY lane
configuration.  The PHY binding and driver already accept the dedicated
compatible, but the SM8250 MDSS parent schema and the board compatible list
must accept it as well.

Signed-off-by: TB371FC Linux port maintainers <tb371fc-desktop@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml          | 1 +
 .../devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8250-mdss.yaml | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
index e8d2a77a2a08..bf4e62e59e54 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
@@ -1055,5 +1055,6 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - lenovo,tb371fc
               - qcom,qrb5165-rb5
               - qcom,sm8250-hdk
               - qcom,sm8250-mtp
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8250-mdss.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8250-mdss.yaml
index 3fb63d820a31..67f51b7f129f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8250-mdss.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8250-mdss.yaml
@@ -78,7 +78,9 @@ patternProperties:
 
     properties:
       compatible:
-        const: qcom,dsi-phy-7nm
+        enum:
+          - lenovo,tb371fc-dsi-phy-7nm
+          - qcom,dsi-phy-7nm
 
 required:
   - compatible
